  "usage_note": "**Mostly** usually goes before the main verb (*We mostly stay in*), after **be** (*They are mostly students*), or before the word or phrase it limits (*mostly in the evening*). Before a noun, the word is **most**, not **mostly**: *most people*.",
  "learner_errors": [
    {
      "incorrect": "Mostly people like this song.",
      "correct": "Most people like this song.",
      "note": "Before a noun, use the determiner **most**; **mostly** goes with a verb or a phrase."
    },
    {
      "incorrect": "The room was mostly of the time empty.",
      "correct": "The room was empty most of the time.",
      "note": "The phrase is **most of the time**; **mostly** alone already means *most of the time*."
    }
